meta-duo-os
===========

Yocto/OpenEmbedded layer for Duo-OS, a small Linux distribution for the Milk-V
Duo family of RISC-V boards:

  - Milk-V Duo      (Sophgo CV1800B, 64MB RAM)  MACHINE = "milkv-duo"
  - Milk-V Duo256M  (Sophgo SG2002)             MACHINE = "milkv-duo256m"
  - Milk-V DuoS     (Sophgo SG2000)             MACHINE = "milkv-duos"

This layer provides the distro configuration, the image recipe and a few
board-specific customizations. The machine definitions and BSP come from
meta-riscv.

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Dependencies
 II. Adding the meta-duo-os layer to your build
III. Building the image
 IV. Contents
  V. Patches


I. Dependencies
===============

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  layers: meta
  branch: master

  URI: https://github.com/riscv/meta-riscv
  branch: master

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded
  layers: meta-oe
  branch: master

II. Adding the meta-duo-os layer to your build
==============================================

From an initialized build environment:

  bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-openembedded/meta-oe
  bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-riscv
  bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-duo-os

III. Building the image
=======================

Set the distro and machine in conf/local.conf or bitbake-config-build
fragments:

  DISTRO = "duo-os"
  MACHINE = "milkv-duo"

Then build the image:

  bitbake milkv-duo-os-image

Write the resulting .wic image to an SD card. On first boot the root partition
is grown to fill the card.

IV. Contents
============

Distro (conf/distro/duo-os.conf)
  - Minimal DISTRO_FEATURES: acl, ipv4, ipv6, keyboard, vfat.
  - systemd as the init manager, except on the original Milk-V Duo, which
    uses musl and sysvinit to better fit in 64MB of RAM.

Image (milkv-duo-os-image)
  - SSH server (OpenSSH, or Dropbear on the Milk-V Duo), opkg package
    management, fastfetch, libgpiod tools and duo-pinmux.
  - NTP time sync with busybox ntpd on the Milk-V Duo.

Recipes and appends
  - resize-rootfs: grows the root partition and filesystem on first boot
    (works with systemd and sysvinit).
  - duo-pinmux: Milk-V pin multiplexing tool
    (https://milkv.io/docs/duo/application-development/pinmux).
  - linux-mainline: Ethernet device tree overlay, LEDs and GPIO line names
    for the Milk-V Duo, /proc/config.gz, and some unused options disabled.
  - u-boot: device tree overlay support and the U-Boot environment stored
    on the FAT boot partition.
  - base-files: custom per-board motd.
  - init-ifupdown: DHCP on eth0.

V. Patches
==========

Please submit patches against the meta-duo-os layer to the maintainer:

